@PointClass size(-8.0 -8.0 -8.0, 8.0 8.0 8.0) color(204 204 204) = water_endless : "Point-placed water. The point's position is exactly where the water surface sits — the water spawns as one giant plane centered on that point and fades into the distance with a fake horizon curvature, giving the feeling of an endless body of water. Uses the same enter/exit submersion behavior (screen tint, splash sound, is-in-water state) as regular water.

Properties:
- color: Water tint color (default blue-ish).
- depth: How far down the water's collision volume extends below the surface, for submersion detection (default 1000.0).
- instant_kill: When enabled, kills the player/enemies instantly on contact instead of behaving as swimmable water.
- radius: Half-size of the water plane and its collision volume in world units (default 20000.0).
- teleport_name: Name of a target_generic marker to teleport the player to on contact (only used if you want a portal-like water surface instead of plain swimmable water)." 
[
